SUMMARY: Music's Marionette: An immersive evening of live classical music
  and animation
DESCRIPTION:Join clarinetist and multimedia artist Nikki Pet for Music’s 
 Marionette\, a striking program that joins live classical music and proje
 cted animation. Inspired by Fantasia\, Pet’s original animations unfold a
 longside the music\, illuminating and extending the expressive world of e
 ach work through color\, motion\, and image. However\, what further sets 
 this performance apart is the technology powering it: a responsive system
 \, developed at IU\, that lets the visuals dynamically shift and flow in 
 response to the live music. The result is a concert unlike any other: whe
 re music and image together transform the experience in ways neither coul
 d achieve alone.\n\nRefreshments will be provided! Student tickets $5\, n
 on-student $12.50\, available for purchase at the door or via Eventbrite:
  www.eventbrite.com/e/musics-marionette-tickets-1985882544148 https://www
 .eventbrite.com/e/musics-marionette-tickets-1985882544148
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Music,Visual-Arts
