SUMMARY:Prepare to Practice Workshop Series: Legislative History Research
DESCRIPTION:Join Jennifer Bryan Morgan\, Government Information Librarian
 \, and Morgan Kelly\, Student Engagement Librarian\, for a legislative hi
 story research workshop! This session is designed to prepare you to condu
 ct legislative history research for your summer assignments.Looking forwa
 rd to the end of exams and the start of your summer employment? Consider 
 attending the Jerome Hall Law Library's "Prepare to Practice" workshop se
 ssions!Each year\, the Jerome Hall Law Library offers a series of worksho
 ps and information sessions to help students prepare for their summer pos
 itions. These sessions offer Maurer students an opportunity to review\, r
 efresh\, and refine their legal research techniques as they prepare for t
 heir summer roles. Each workshop focuses on reinforcing foundational skil
 ls\, exploring effective research approaches\, and helping students feel 
 more confident in tackling real-world research tasks.If you have any ques
 tions\, please contact Morgan Kelly\, Student Engagement Librarian\, via 
 email atkellyms@iu.edu.
