CATEGORIES:Athletics
DESCRIPTION:The World Basketball Analytics Club will host the NBA Front Of
 fice Analytics Challenge\, where members take on the role of an NBA gener
 al manager and develop a data-driven offseason strategy for a selected te
 am. Participants will analyze roster construction\, player performance\, 
 and advanced basketball metrics to evaluate team strengths and weaknesses
  and identify potential free agency or trade opportunities. Using analyti
 cs such as offensive and defensive ratings\, efficiency metrics\, and oth
 er advanced statistics\, teams will create strategic recommendations to i
 mprove their franchise’s future performance. Students will have 45 minute
 s to work and then will present their findings to the club\, explaining t
 heir roster decisions and analytical insights. This event allows students
  to apply the analytics concepts and frameworks they have been studying w
 hile also developing critical thinking\, collaboration\, and presentation
  skills. This event offers a fun celebration and end-of-year experience w
 hile incorporating everything members have been learning throughout the y
 ear.\n**If you are not a current member of WBAC and plan on attending\, p
 lease email jackdost@iu.edu**\n\nHosted by: World Basketball Analytics Cl
 ub\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.
 edu/event/12400629
DTEND:20260413T224500Z
DTSTAMP:20260411T143034Z
DTSTART:20260413T213000Z
LOCATION:Ballantine Hall\, BH 110
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:NBA Front Office Analytics Challenge
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12400629
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12400629
X-HOSTS:World Basketball Analytics Club
END:VEVENT
