BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU beINvolved Student Orgs": "https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12391752"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_campuslabs
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Social Event
CATEGORIES:Leadership & Engagement
CATEGORIES:Intellectual Wellness
DESCRIPTION:The Organization for Non-Traditional Students at IU Bloomingto
 n and the Midwest (North America) Chapter of Accepted Society are collabo
 rating on an in-person Study Hall and social event! Please join us on Sun
 day\, April 19th\, at the IMU (room TBA)! Bring your laptop and anything 
 you need to work on. Please reach out to the ONTS President and Accepted 
 Society Midwest Chapter Host\, Meranda Cree Prince\, if you have any ques
 tions or would like to receive updates on this event! (email: mcprince@iu
 .edu) 📚👩‍💻📝 Event itinerary is as follows:\nBrunch in the Tudor Room 
 at the Indiana Memorial Union: 11:00 a.m. - 1:00 p.m.\nBreak time! Feel f
 ree to explore the IMU and downtown Bloomington\, or grab a coffee: 1:15 
 p.m. - 2:15 p.m.\nStudy Hall / Co-working in the IMU Tree Suites (room TB
 D): 2:30 p.m. - 6:00 p.m.\nDinner: If scholars would like to stay in town
  for the evening\, feel free to coordinate with one another! The IMU has 
 hotel rooms available in the Biddle Hotel\, and there are several other h
 otels or Airbnb options downtown. Plenty of great spots for dinner are wi
 thin walking distance of the IMU. \nNB: Parking is available in the IMU p
 ay lot or across the street at the Poplars Garage.\n📍Indiana Memorial Un
 ion: 900 E 7th St\, Bloomington\, IN 47405\n\nHosted by: Organization for
  Non-Traditional Students at Indiana University\n\nAdditional Information
  can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12391752
DTEND:20260419T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260411T143034Z
DTSTART:20260419T183000Z
LOCATION:IMU Bryan Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
