X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Cicada Cinema": "https://cicadacinema.com/products/pillion-april-22-back-door-8pm"}
X-SOURCE-ID:cicada_cinema
SUMMARY:Pillion
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T200000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T200000
UID:shopify-8208657940524@cicadacinema.com
DESCRIPTION:$8.00 - Tickets for the 8 PM screening of PILLION 2026 • UK 
 • 107 minutes • dir. Harry Lighton Wednesday\, April 22nd at The Back 
 Door (207 S College Ave) $8 | 21+ Showtime: 8 pm TRAILER Synopsis : In his
  unorthodox queer romance\, first-time feature director Harry Lighton has 
 fashioned something highly improbable: a film about a sadomasochistic rela
 tionship that is both transgressive and disarming. Harry Melling plays the
  mild Colin\, whose gayness is happily accepted by his parents (Lesley Sha
 rp and Douglas Hodge) and who is most extroverted when singing in a barber
 shop quartet. When this sweet-natured square catches the eye of strapping\
 , leather-clad biker Ray (Alexander Skarsgård) at the local pub\, he find
 s himself entering a submissive role—both domestic and erotic—for the 
 inscrutable beauty who brings him both satisfaction and confusion\, pain a
 nd pleasure. As their affair continues\, Colin must decide what he wants a
 nd needs—and who he really is. Comic without ever descending into judgme
 nt of its characters\, Pillion is a beguiling inquiry into the social and 
 sexual performances of masculinity\, featuring fearless work from Melling 
 and Skarsgård.
LOCATION:Back Door
URL:https://cicadacinema.com/products/pillion-april-22-back-door-8pm
