SUMMARY:Let's Look Together: Scholarship Search Lab
DESCRIPTION:This session offers a focused\, low‑pressure environment wh
 ere you can search for scholarships using trusted websites\, ask question
 s\, and start building a list of opportunities to apply for—no applicat
 ions are due during the workshop.During this session\, you will:Use reput
 able scholarship search tools to find current opportunities  Learn strate
 gies for filtering and identifying scholarships you may be eligible for  
 Save and organize scholarships to apply for later  Gain a clearer underst
 anding of common scholarship requirements and timelines  Who should atten
 d:  Pre-business students and friendsWhat to bring (optional):Resume or l
 ist of activities\, awards\, and work experience  Basic academic informat
 ion (major\, GPA\, expected graduation year)    Staff will be available t
 hroughout the hour to answer questions and help you stay on track. Even i
 f you've never applied for a scholarship before\, this is a great place t
 o start.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This session offers a focused\, low‑p
 ressure environment where you can search for scholarships using trusted w
 ebsites\, ask questions\, and start building a list of opportunities to a
 pply for—no applications are due during the workshop.</p><p><strong>Dur
 ing this session\, you will:</strong></p><ul><li>Use reputable scholarshi
 p search tools to find current opportunities  </li><li>Learn strategies f
 or filtering and identifying scholarships you may be eligible for  </li><
 li>Save and organize scholarships to apply for later  </li><li>Gain a cle
 arer understanding of common scholarship requirements and timelines  </li
 ></ul><p><strong>Who should attend:</strong><br />  Pre-business students
  and friends</p><p><strong>What to bring (optional):</strong></p><ul><li>
 Resume or list of activities\, awards\, and work experience  </li><li>Bas
 ic academic information (major\, GPA\, expected graduation year)  </li></
 ul><p>  Staff will be available throughout the hour to answer questions a
 nd help you stay on track. Even if you've never applied for a scholarship
  before\, this is a great place to start.</p>
