BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2161704-exploring-music-in-art", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2161704-exploring-music-in-art", "IU Jacobs School of Music": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2161704-exploring-music-in-art"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2161704-exploring-music-in-art"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Arts & Humanities Institute, IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20260503T173000Z
DTEND:20260503T183000Z
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art - Room Number: Check in at the informatio
 n desk on the first floor
SUMMARY:Exploring Music in Art
DESCRIPTION:Depending on what's on view\, this tour may include a Māori 
 flute\, Shiva (Lord of the Dance)\, drums from the Austral Islands and Ne
 w Ireland\, a Mayan bell\, a Kango whistle\, a Lumbo bow lute\, a Mangbet
 a friction drum\, an Egyptian castanet\, sculptures of seated female Chin
 ese musicians playing a pipa and a piaxiao\, a biwat flute stop\, and a g
 ope board to play music from New Guinea sent to space on Voyager's Golden
  Record.&#160\;&#160\;  About your guide:  Kathie Durkel has volunteered 
 as a Guide at the Eskenazi Museum of Art for more than ten years. She is 
 the 2023 recipient of the Meier Award in recognition for her exemplary se
 rvice\, enthusiasm\,and commitment to learning. She enjoys creating thema
 tic tours\, like this one.&#160\;  &#160\;  Know Before You GoSpace is av
 ailable for the first 12 people to check in with Guest Services on the da
 y. Drop by the information desk on the first floor of the museum when you
  arrive.Strollers are welcome. A small handbag may be carried at your sid
 e. Backpacks and large bags will need to be stored before touring. Learn 
 more aboutmuseum guidelines.If you park in the Indiana Memorial Union par
 king lot\, Guest Services can validate your parking voucher for a discoun
 t.Read aboutwhere to find us and where to park\,
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Depending on what's on view\, this tour
  may include a Māori flute\, Shiva (Lord of the Dance)\, drums from the 
 Austral Islands and New Ireland\, a Mayan bell\, a Kango whistle\, a Lumb
 o bow lute\, a Mangbeta friction drum\, an Egyptian castanet\, sculptures
  of seated female Chinese musicians playing a pipa and a piaxiao\, a biwa
 t flute stop\, and a gope board to play <span class="markr71qc27yz" data-
 markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">music</
 span> from New Guinea sent to space on Voyager's Golden Record.&#160\;&#1
 60\;</p><h3>  About your guide:</h3><p>  Kathie Durkel has volunteered as
  a Guide at the Eskenazi Museum of Art for more than ten years. She is th
 e 2023 recipient of the Meier Award in recognition for <span data-contras
 t="none">her exemplary service\, enthusiasm\,</span><span data-contrast="
 none">and commitment to learning</span><span data-contrast="none">. She e
 njoys creating thematic tours\, like this one.&#160\;</span></p><p>  &#16
