SUMMARY: Your Name Means Dream by Jose Rivera
DESCRIPTION:AI is hauntingly current and a topic that urges us to examine
  its impact.\nWill AI robots soon replace human caregivers for the elderl
 y? With emotionally-charged narrative and poetic dialogue\, José Rivera e
 xamines how we live and form our sense of self in a world that’s increasi
 ngly saturated with technology. It challenges all people\, all identities
  and all faiths. How do we apply morals\, values and ethics when we intro
 duce machine over human?\n\nTheatre legend Diane Kondrat\, who moved west
  after performing theatre for 27 years in Bloomington\, is returning to s
 tar in this production. The role of AI caregiver Stacy will be played by 
 Valerie C. Kilmer who is making her debut with JTB.\n\nWith an extraordin
 ary team of artists and a fascinating topic\, this production promises to
  be a sell-out!
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Theatre
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62fb9509b27fd5
 06428328ed/69a723444d50ac5b2c92ce1c/scaled_896.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:AI is hauntingly current and a topic that urges us t
 o examine its impact. Will AI robots soon replace human caregivers for th
 e elderly? With...
X-TKF-PROMOTION-BUTTON;label=Dream Tickets;skip_details=false:https://www
 .jewishtheatrebloomington.com/
LOCATION:Waldron Rose Firebay\,122 South Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
  47404\, USA
CREATED:20260303T180702Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T173755Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260303T180702Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sycamore Land Trust": "https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2026/04/hike-the-trust-canyon-forest-nature-preserve/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sycamore_land_trust
SUMMARY:Hike the Trust: Canyon Forest Nature Preserve
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260510T090000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260510T110000
UID:c9ea4044c14c5793161c1df574548ba3@sycamorelandtrust.org
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided hike as part of our Hike the Trust series
  at Canyon Forest Nature Preserve\, a rugged and scenic 68-acre preserve. 
 Its deep ravines and sandstone outcrops are part of Greene County’s anci
 ent bedrock\, where resistant sandstones and underlying shale have been sc
 ulpted over millions of years to form dramatic canyons and slopes that sup
 port diverse plant communities\, from orchids and ferns to woodland trees.
  Along the way\, we’ll tie together how the geology influences soil\, wa
 ter flow\, and plant distribution\, helping you see the connection between
  rocks\, soils\, forests\, and ecological diversity in one of Indiana’s 
 most interesting natural areas.
LOCATION:Canyon Forest Nature Preserve
URL:https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2026/04/hike-the-trust-canyon-forest-nat
 ure-preserve/
X-SOURCE:Sycamore Land Trust
END:VEVENT
