X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2101230-homeschool-day-america-250"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_eskenazi_museum
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art
DTSTART:20260514T140000Z
DTEND:20260514T150000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: America 250
DESCRIPTION:Travel back in time with us to America in 1776 to meet George
  Washington and see the Declaration of Independence up close. Together\, 
 we'll explore the art and stories that shaped our nation's founding. Afte
 rwards\, we'll create our own colonial-inspired artwork in the studio\, r
 eflecting on the theme of "What America Means to Me."Know Before You Go: 
  Meet us on the 1st floor of the museum at 10 a.m. Together\, we'll drop 
 off personal items in the Simpson Center for Education before exploring t
 he galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll
  head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own master
 pieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chapero
 nes required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for 
 every 6 children.Parking Information:  The museum is in the pedestrian di
 strict of campus with several parking options nearby. The Indiana Memoria
 l Union lot (900 E. 7th Street) is just a 5-minute walk diagonal to the m
 useum\, and visitors can receive 40% off parking validation at the museum
 's guest services desk. The East Garage (105 N. Eagleson Ave.) and Fee La
 ne Garage (709 N. Fee Lane) are also convenient\, about an 8–10 minute 
 walk. Learn more about parking on the Bloomington campus here (https://pa
 rking.indiana.edu/facilities/index.html).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Travel back in time with us to America 
 in 1776 to meet George Washington and see the Declaration of Independence
  up close. Together\, we'll explore the art and stories that shaped our n
 ation's founding. Afterwards\, we'll create our own colonial-inspired art
 work in the studio\, reflecting on the theme of "What America Means to Me
 ."</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us on the 1st 
 floor of the museum at 10 a.m. Together\, we'll drop off personal items i
 n the Simpson Center for Education before exploring the galleries. After 
 seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Ro
 ehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget
  to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. Chaperones required.
  We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 child
 ren.</p><p><strong>Parking Information:</strong></p><p>  The museum is in
  the pedestrian district of campus with several parking options nearby. T
 he Indiana Memorial Union lot (900 E. 7th Street) is just a 5-minute walk
  diagonal to the museum\, and visitors can receive 40% off parking valida
 tion at the museum's guest services desk. The East Garage (105 N. Eagleso
 n Ave.) and Fee Lane Garage (709 N. Fee Lane) are also convenient\, about
  an 8–10 minute walk. Learn more about parking on the Bloomington campu
 s <a href="https://parking.indiana.edu/facilities/index.html">here</a>.</
 p>
