DESCRIPTION:At the Rev. Ernest D. Butler Park Community Garden.<br>Registra
 tion required\; $15/person.<br>Register by May 12 at <a href="https://webtr
 ac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/web/search.html?Primarycode=265201">https://w
 ebtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/web/search.html?Primarycode=265201</a><br
 >Join us for an evening in the garden learning the proper techniques for pr
 opagating our culinary herb garden\, before sharing the bounty. Each partic
 ipant will come away with the knowledge of how to make cuttings from mature
  plants\, where to best plant the cuttings\, and how to use their unique fl
 avor profiles. All participants will take home their own miniature herb gar
 den to start the season. Come with questions and leave with herbs. Children
  under 12 yrs. must be accompanied by an adult.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260409T151139Z
LOCATION:Rev. Ernest D. Butler Park\, 812 W 9th St\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
 \, USA
