BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:btonline_events
X-SOURCE:Btonline Events
DTSTART:20260605T210000Z
DTEND:20260606T120000Z
DTSTAMP:20260411T143022Z
UID:892b7db0-372a-4f7b-8bf9-558c7fade5e2@bloomington-online
CREATED:20260325T121608Z
DESCRIPTION:Beacon's Solidarity Sleepout — Sleep out so others don't have t
 o!\n\nJoin us on June 5th at 5pm until June 6th at 8am on the greenspace at
  First United Methodist Church in Bloomington. Participants will choose to 
 sleep outside for one night to stand in solidarity with those who don't hav
 e that choice.\n\nBy asking their friends and family to sponsor them\, part
 icipants will raise essential funds for Beacon's emergency shelter — the la
 rgest year-round emergency shelter for women in our area.\n\nLet's acknowle
 dge the realities of homelessness and inspire empathy and action as we come
  together to build a community where everyone has a safe place to sleep and
  the support they need on their path home.\n\nTo sign up or view more infor
 mation\, visit: sleepout.info\n\nContact: Isabella Frieze | isabella@beacon
 inc.org | 812-496-4734
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T121625Z
LOCATION:First United Methodist Church\, 219 E 4th St\, Bloomington\, IN 47
 408\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Beacon's Solidarity Sleepout
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Boys & Girls Club Bloomington": "https://bgcbloomington.org/event/lemonade-day-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bgc_bloomington
X-SOURCE:Boys & Girls Club Bloomington
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260606
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260607
DTSTAMP:20260411T102955
CREATED:20251031T180512Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251031T180512Z
UID:14108-1780704000-1780790399@bgcbloomington.org
SUMMARY:Lemonade Day 2026
DESCRIPTION:Lemonade Day is a free\, fun\, experiential learning program that teaches youth how to start\, own and operate their own business – a lemonade stand. \nThe foremost objective of Lemonade Day is to empower youth to take ownership of their lives and become productive members of society – the business leaders\, social advocates\, volunteers\, and forward thinking citizens of tomorrow. \nEach child that registers receives access to Lemonopolis\, our FREE and FUN online curriculum that teaches them Lemonade Day lessons like creating budgets\, setting profit-making goals\, serving customers\, repaying investors\, and giving back to the community. Along the way\, they acquire skills in goal-setting\, problem solving\, and gain self-esteem critical for future success. They also receive additional digital content from local sponsors and experts on topics like Building a Lemonade Stand\, Recipe Exploration\, Marketing\, and more!
URL:https://bgcbloomington.org/event/lemonade-day-2026/
LOCATION:IN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://bgcbloomington.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/lemda.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Boys & Girls Clubs of Bloomington":MAILTO:info@bgcbloomington.org
END:VEVENT
