BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sycamore Land Trust": "https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2025/08/seed-collection-at-powell-preserve/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sycamore_land_trust
SUMMARY:Seed Collection at Powell Preserve
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260929T130000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260929T150000
UID:f6c3fc8099828288f57daa1f861c0876@sycamorelandtrust.org
DESCRIPTION:Join Education Director Saige Sentell for a special volunteer 
 opportunity to learn how to ethically harvest and clean seeds for habitat 
 restoration projects\, targeting native prairie species such as prairie co
 neflower\, bergamot\, coneflower\, common milkweed\, big bluestem\, hollow
  Joe Pye\, common boneset\, blackhaw viburnum and more. The seeds you coll
 ect will be used in educational programming throughout our 26-county servi
 ce area and in future restoration projects at our preserves. Participants 
 will be working off-trail in tall vegetation. Long sleeves\, long pants\, 
 sturdy shoes\, and sun protection are required. Powell Preserve is not ope
 n to the public. Registration is required.
LOCATION:Powell Preserve
URL:https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2025/08/seed-collection-at-powell-preser
 ve/
X-SOURCE:Sycamore Land Trust
END:VEVENT
