SUMMARY:Seed Collection at Touch the Earth Natural Area
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261002T130000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261002T150000
UID:67ae663406d792671e2ddc0b7daaaf43@sycamorelandtrust.org
DESCRIPTION:Join Education Director Saige Sentell for a special volunteer 
 opportunity to learn how to ethically harvest and clean seeds for habitat 
 restoration projects\, targeting native prairie species such as big bluest
 em\, false blue indigo\, and more. The seeds you collect will be used in e
 ducational programming throughout our 26-county service area and in future
  restoration projects at our preserves. Participants will be working off-t
 rail in tall vegetation. Long sleeves\, long pants\, sturdy shoes\, and su
 n protection are required.
LOCATION:Touch the Earth Natural Area
URL:https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2025/08/seed-collection-at-touch-the-ear
 th-natural-area/
