X-SOURCE:IU Moving Image Archive
DTSTART:20261210T143500Z
DTEND:20261210T155000Z
DTSTAMP:20261210T000000Z
SUMMARY:CMLT-C 291: STUDIES IN NON-WESTERN FILM (Izabela Potapowicz)
DESCRIPTION:Emphasis on non-Western film in relation to literary and 
 cultural texts. Films may be studied as adaptations of literary works\, as 
 reworkings of generic or ideological traditions\, and in their engagement 
 with the aesthetics of non-Western theater and Hollywood. Focus on one 
 regional tradition (African\, Asian\, Middle Eastern) each time the course 
 is offered.
LOCATION:Wells Screening Room (ground floor\, within Media Services)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jamie Thomas":MAILTO:jt85@iu.edu
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-5914-16651839
URL:https://iub.libcal.com/event/16651839
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Moving Image Archive": "https://iub.libcal.com/event/16434969"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_libcal_screening_room
X-SOURCE:IU Moving Image Archive
DTSTART:20261210T174500Z
DTEND:20261210T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261210T000000Z
SUMMARY:LATS-L 111: LATINO FILM: AN INTRODUCTION AND OVERVIEW (John Nieto-Phillips)
DESCRIPTION:This course examines U.S. films by and/or about Hispanics and 
 Latinos/as (i.e. Mexican-American/Chicano\, Puerto Rican/Boricus\, and 
 Cuban-American.) Throughout the semester we will explore the complex 
 relationship between the constructions of Latino/a identities\, Latino/a 
 stereo-types\, and the circumstances which Latinos encounter in the U.S. as 
 portrayed in film.\n
LOCATION:Wells Screening Room (ground floor\, within Media Services)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jamie Thomas":MAILTO:jt85@iu.edu
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-5914-16434969
URL:https://iub.libcal.com/event/16434969
END:VEVENT
